# Build outputs
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.ELF
*.efi
*.EFI
*.bin
# ...but pwbreach.bin is SOURCE, not a build output. It is a generated table of
# FNV-1a hashes of breached passwords, include_bytes!-ed by
# kernel/rustkern/pwpolicy.rs and named in kernel/Makefile RUST_BLOBS, so a
# clean clone CANNOT BUILD THE RUST KERNEL LIBRARY without it. The 2026-08-28
# public push shipped without it: the release gate had cleared the file, then
# 'git add -A' skipped it silently on this very line and nothing warned. A
# gate proves nothing about a push if .gitignore sits between them.
!kernel/rustkern/pwbreach.bin
kernel/kernel.elf
boot/uefi/BOOTX64.EFI
userland/libc/libc.a
userland/libc/crt0.o
userland/libgl/libgl.a

# Rust build trees
target/
**/target/

# Disk images and release artifacts
*.img
*.img.gz
*.iso
boot_disk.img
.stage-mnt/

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Never commit local credentials or machine-specific config.
# The disk template under disk/CONFIG carries only non-secret defaults
# (autologin, menu, theme). Anything holding a real key, token or password
# belongs outside this repository.
*.KEY
*.key
AUTHKEYS
SHADOW
SSH.CFG
EXTSVC.CFG
